  "name": "a batchSize above the wire's limit still sends at most 100 events",
  "source": "packages/shared/src/events.ts eventBatchSchema \u2014 z.array(clientEventSchema).min(1).max(100). Both SDKs declared MAX_BATCH_SIZE = 100 with a comment saying exactly that and neither enforced it, so an app configuring a larger batchSize had every batch answered 400. A 400 is not retryable, so poison isolation then re-sent the events one at a time: nothing lost, and every flush costing 1 + N requests for the life of the install. Found by scripts/check-unreferenced.mjs, which reported the constant as declared and called by nothing.",
